refuse-fstab-no-target — the debian-boot-root-swap-bios donor plus an fstab line
"/dev/sdc1 /data ext4 defaults 0 2" whose disk is not in the inventory (dev=-) and has no nofail.
Exercises R10: an fstab spec without a target and without nofail is refused (exit 4); with
nofail it would be removed with a WARN instead (asserted on the fly by the test).
